      ":question/id": "8aed94b7-6b73-5e2c-b06b-87988e996be0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\cos{(8 x )} + 8 y \\sin{(8 x )} + 8 \\sin{(16 x )}=0\\,.\n$$\n\nAssume $\\cos{(8 x )}\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\cos{(8 x )} + 8 y \\sin{(8 x )} + 8 \\sin{(16 x )}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\cos{(8 x )} + 8 y \\sin{(8 x )}=- 8 \\sin{(16 x )} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + \\frac{8 y \\sin{(8 x )}}{\\cos{(8 x )}}=- \\frac{8 \\sin{(16 x )}}{\\cos{(8 x )}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 8 y \\tan{(8 x )}=\\frac{- 16 \\sin{(8 x )}\\cos{(8 x )}}{\\cos{(8 x )}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(8 \\tan{(8 x )})}_{P(x)}y=\\underbrace{- 16 \\sin{(8 x )}}_{Q(x)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=8 \\tan{(8 x )}$ and $Q(x)=- 16 \\sin{(8 x )}.$",
